# 24. Cybersecurity Connection

Linux fundamentals matter because security work constantly involves interacting with the filesystem.

Examples:

```text
Investigating logs
        ↓
       less

Finding configuration files
        ↓
       filesystem navigation

Investigating suspicious files
        ↓
       ls / cat / file operations

Examining user environments
        ↓
       home directories

Investigating credentials/configuration
        ↓
       hidden files and directories

Managing security tools
        ↓
       filesystem + permissions
```

Linux is not just another topic to memorize.

It is the environment in which a large amount of cybersecurity work happens.
